      "id": 1,
      "text": "Winnsboro, Louisiana, was named after Senator John Winn, who founded the settlement in 1854 and helped create Franklin Parish in 1843.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Winnsboro,_Louisiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1846, the town—originally spelled Winnsborough—was officially designated the seat of government for the newly formed Franklin Parish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Winnsboro,_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The railroad’s arrival in 1876 shifted Winnsboro’s economy from timber and basic crops to a diversified agricultural base that later included peaches, strawberries, cattle, poultry, and dairy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Winnsboro,_Louisiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Winnsboro experiences a humid subtropical climate, with long, hot summers and short, mild winters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
